    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup construction today is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who sits at a dominant 81.67 score against Singer. His elite 8% BvP boost, combined with a favorable park factor and a spot in the #2 hole, makes him our primary offensive engine. We also see high-efficiency upside from **Cal Raleigh** (75.22) and **Daulton Varsho** (69.94). **Cal Raleigh** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Lauer and a strong order position, while **Daulton Varsho** exploits a high-xERA opponent in Littell, leveraging his speed profile to maintain value in our scarcity-driven SB framework despite the moderate risks associated with the pitcher\u2019s strikeout profile. **Gleyber Torres** also warrants attention as a top-tier start; despite facing a lefty, his lead-off spot and a substantial 13% platoon edge push him to a 67.46 score.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today\u2019s card was the exclusion of **Luis Arraez** (40.59). While he narrowly missed the 40.0 \"Zebras Floor,\" his projection was crippled by a matchup against the elite Pannone (0.00 xERA). In a 5x5 format where we prioritize efficiency, the combination of a low-strikeout pitcher and a suppressed run-scoring environment forced the optimizer to prefer the upside of hitters like **Jonathan Aranda** or **Gavin Sheets**, who carry higher volatility but better ceiling potential against their respective opponents. \n\nRegarding roster risks, several spots remain contingent on finalized lineups. **Yainer Diaz**, **Masyn Winn**, and **Lawrence Butler** all carry \"Lineup Pending\" tags, and while their current scores assume specific spots in the order, any movement toward the bottom of the lineup could trigger a re-evaluation of their start eligibility. Furthermore, we are keeping a close eye on **Taylor Ward**; while he is currently active, he faces Skubal, an elite arm (2.62 xERA) that dragged his score down to 53.15 despite a positive platoon advantage. We are comfortable with these assignments, provided the weather holds and managers do not shuffle these hitters into defensive-minded lineup configurations.",
